#### 2.4 Global Accessor

For ergonomic use across the codebase, provide a module-level function that returns a lazily-initialized global instance. This avoids threading a `BivvyPaths` through every call site.

```rust
use std::sync::OnceLock;

static PATHS: OnceLock<BivvyPaths> = OnceLock::new();

/// Get the global paths instance.
///
/// Initializes on first call using `BivvyPaths::detect()`.
/// Panics if no XDG directory and no BIVVY_HOME is available
/// (this should never happen on supported platforms).
pub fn paths() -> &'static BivvyPaths {
    PATHS.get_or_init(|| {
        BivvyPaths::detect()
            .expect("Could not determine Bivvy paths: no home directory found")
    })
}

/// Override the global paths instance (for testing).
///
