The centralized approach eliminates fallbacks entirely: `BivvyPaths::detect()` returns `Option<Self>` and `paths()` panics if `None`. On all supported platforms (macOS, Linux, Windows), `dirs::config_dir()`, `dirs::data_local_dir()`, and `dirs::cache_dir()` return `Some`. The only scenario where they return `None` is if `HOME` is unset on Unix or `FOLDERID_RoamingAppData` fails on Windows, which are truly broken environments where Bivvy cannot operate.

